  "title": "addr_resolv: Format-truncation",
  "description": "When constructing a name for a EUI-48 from an OUI plus the last\nthree bytes, truncate if necessary from the OUI name, not the bytes.\n(The OUI resolved name should never be that long, because it's the\nshort name, but gcc doesn't know that.)\n\nPing #20175",
